PLR 3.3.2 stateful data descriptor, FORWARD-REFERENCE order: the
descriptor class (Pos) is defined before the field-owning class (C), so
when Pos.__get__/__set__ convert, no registered class declares `_v` yet
and `obj._v` bakes to nondet. The __set__ routing + boxing are correct
(see data-descriptor-stateful, which verifies when the field class is
registered first). Completion needs registering all class struct fields
before converting method bodies (conversion-ordering fix). KNOWNBUG states
the PLR-correct outcome.
